Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-17-2001||10:12 PM||||ok, so I am installing a cd player in my car, soon hopefully, What wiring harness do I need to buy?  and is there anything else I need to buy or should buy?  thanks!<P>  *~Paul Ventimiglia<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic2222.jpg"> <BR>NEW pics are coming SOON hopefully... geez!||||reg||1
Z||000001||watts||11-17-2001||10:21 PM||||To keep your stock harness all nice (don't cut it up!!!), pick up one of the many harness adaptors out there, along with a mounting kit (to allow the smaller DIN chassis to fit into the humungo hole).<P>Personally, I laid the harness out on my bench, ran heat shrink down each wire, soldered the kit harness onto my deck harness, shrunk everything, then tie-wrapped about every 6".  Makes for a very nice and tidy package.  <P>Install all the above onto the mounting hardware kit.  Take out the appropriate screws that hols the stock deck in, and swap over the metal brackets from your stock deck onto the mounting kit.  Install the new deck and you're done!  Plug and play.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
